# Frontend architecture

```
src/app/          # providers, router, shell entry
src/features/     # radar, brief, competitors, sources, pricing, contact
src/shared/       # api, ui, lib, config
```

## Rules

- Put page logic under `features/<name>/pages/`; reusable pieces in `features/<name>/components/` or `shared/ui/`.
- API calls only through `shared/api` (TanStack Query in pages/hooks — do not scatter raw `fetch`).
- Routes live in `app/router.tsx`; nav labels in `shared/config/nav.ts`.
- TypeScript strict: no `any` unless bridging messy API data with a short comment.

## UI

- Match existing RadArt shell (AppShell, badges, filters, trend groups) — extend, don’t invent a second design system.
- Agency dashboard: clear hierarchy, French product copy where screens already use FR.
- Responsive: desktop + mobile usable; avoid clutter and duplicate KPI walls.
- New screens: one job per page section (radar ≠ brief ≠ sources).

## Data UX

- Show loading / empty / error states for radar, brief results, and source status.
- Refresh / collection actions must reflect backend status, not fake success.
